.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt NEWGRP 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm newgrp
.Nd switch to a group and start a shell
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl l
.Op Ar group
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility resolves
.Ar group
from the system group database, verifies that the caller is root, the group's primary member,
or an explicit member, installs the new real and effective group id through the existing libc
credential path, and starts the user's shell.
With no operand it selects the caller's login group from the password database.
A numeric operand is a group id; otherwise it is a group name.
.Pp
The shell is
.Ev SHELL
when set, then the login shell from the password record, then
.Pa /bin/brush .
The options are:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl l
Start the shell as a login shell: the argv[0] name is prefixed with a dash and the login
environment is supplied.
.El
.Pp
A group password is not prompted for in this slice.
A caller who is not a member is denied with
.Dq permission denied: group password is not supported
rather than blocking on the console.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
0 on success, 1 for an unknown group, permission or credential failure, 2 for usage.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr login 1 ,
.Xr su 1
.Sh STANDARDS
A documented subset of POSIX
.Nm newgrp .
Group password prompting, `/etc/gshadow`, user functions and any session manager are
unsupported.
